<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Two polar charts compare wind and wave directions over time from June 2019 to June 2020. Chart a\) displays wind direction and Chart b\) shows wave direction, both using color gradients from yellow to purple, representing different months. Concentric circles indicate direction angles from 50 to 350 degrees.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt <> /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Four line graphs from July 2019 to July 2020. Graph a\) shows wind speed in meters per second ranging from 0 to 12. Graph b\) displays significant wave height in meters ranging from 0 to 6. Graph c\) illustrates the ratio of Ucos\(theta\) to C_P from 0 to 1. Graph d\) depicts theta in degrees ranging from 0 to 150.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Four scatter plots showing wind stress components \(\\\(\\tau_1\\\) and \\\(\\tau_2\\\)\) versus wind speed \(in meters per second\), with data points colored by \\\(U \\cos \\theta / C_d\\\). Panels a and b represent data for June, July, and August \(JJA\) for \\\(\\tau_1\\\) and \\\(\\tau_2\\\), respectively. Panels c and d represent December, January, and February \(DJF\) for \\\(\\tau_1\\\) and \\\(\\tau_2\\\), respectively. The legend indicates the magnitude of \\\(|\\theta|\\\) with varying circle sizes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt <> /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Scatter plots compare \\\(\\tau_1\\\) and \\\(\\tau_x\\\) values for different datasets. Panel a\) JJA, panel b\) DJF. Colored points represent data groups: in a\) blue, red, yellow; in b\) blue, brown, teal. Lines indicate trend directions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Two line graphs compare sea conditions against wind speed in meters per second. Graph a\) for JJA and graph b\) for DJF display four categories: swell opp \(blue\), swell fol&crs \(red\), mixed sea \(teal\), and wind sea \(brown\). Graph a\) shows swell fol&crs declining and mixed sea rising with wind speed. Graph b\) shows swell opp declining, and wind sea rising significantly.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Bar chart showing bias percentages for different inverse wave age categories. Categories include less than zero, zero to 0.5, 0.5 to 0.8, and greater than 0.8. The chart compares WiBF \(black bars\) and WBF \(gray bars\). WiBF shows negative bias for all categories except 0.5 to 0.8, where it is negative at minus 4.2 percent. WBF shows negative bias in the first two categories, less than zero with minus 15.5 percent, zero to 0.5 with minus 10.1 percent, and positive bias in the last two, 0.5 to 0.8 at 6.7 percent and greater than 0.8 at 16.3 percent.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
